WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.420 --> 00:00:02.200
Where do you go once the battle is won?

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:06.180
The third episode of Game of Thrones' eighth
and final season "The Long Night," was all

00:00:06.189 --> 00:00:10.811
sorts of intense and warning, spoilers ahead
with the brutality and bloodshed of the Battle

00:00:10.811 --> 00:00:15.040
of Winterfell nearly taking out our Westerosi
heroes and letting the Night King and his

00:00:15.040 --> 00:00:17.220
army of wights and White Walkers roam free.

00:00:17.690 --> 00:00:22.160
But Arya Stark harnessed her inner ninja,
evoked the spirit of Azor Ahai, and turned

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:25.890
the battle from a losing one to an instant
success when she stabbed the Night King and

00:00:25.890 --> 00:00:28.180
cut off his minions' lifeline in the process.

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:32.910
The side of the living won the Battle of Winterfell,
the dead fell and so too did the Long Night,

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:35.420
and the sun began to rise over Winterfell
once more.

00:00:35.500 --> 00:00:36.500
So what comes next?

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:40.780
With just three episodes of Game of Thrones
left and the perceived greatest threat already

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:42.840
eliminated, how will everyone move forward?

00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:47.000
Thankfully, HBO hasn't left fans totally in
the lurch after Episode 3.

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:50.820
The network released a preview for the upcoming
episode that offers a taste of the events

00:00:50.829 --> 00:00:52.500
to come after the Battle of Winterfell.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:54.600
And boy, are they going to be wild.

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:58.860
In the teaser, Daenerys Targaryen, fresh off
learning her lover Jon Snow is actually her

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:03.340
nephew and the true heir to the Iron Throne,
states that the Great War is over and Last

00:01:03.360 --> 00:01:05.140
War is about to fall upon Westeros.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:07.100
What war might that be, and what will it entail?

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:11.440
Oh, you know, just a casual storming of the
Westerosi capital of King's Landing, where

00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:15.320
Dany will send her depleted army to march
against the reigning queen Cersei Lannister.

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:18.400
The Lannister lioness isn't going to go down
without a fight, of course.

00:01:18.620 --> 00:01:22.760
In the eyes of many, Cersei has gone mad with
power — and with grief over the loss of

00:01:22.760 --> 00:01:24.940
her three children over the course of the
series.

00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:29.800
She may not have dragons, Unsullied soldiers,
the support of very many in Westeros, or those

00:01:29.810 --> 00:01:33.920
elephants she really, really wanted, but Cersei
does have someone who matches her hunger for

00:01:33.920 --> 00:01:35.620
dominance: Euron Greyjoy.

00:01:35.890 --> 00:01:40.340
He's got violence to spare, a fierce loyalty
to Cersei motivated in part by his desire

00:01:40.340 --> 00:01:43.700
to continue their intimate relationship, and
no qualms about killing.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:45.780
Sounds like a perfect match for Cersei, right?

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:50.759
Plus, Cersei has Euron's Iron Fleet and the
Essos sellsword force the Golden Company,

00:01:50.759 --> 00:01:52.670
ringing in at 20,000 strong.

00:01:52.670 --> 00:01:55.240
She's not exactly the underdog in this impending
battle.

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:58.780
Still, Daenerys and company aren't all that
worried about the fight Cersei and Euron will

00:01:58.780 --> 00:01:59.980
put up in King's Landing.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:03.259
The Mother of Dragons makes it clear that
she and those who fought in the Battle of

00:02:03.259 --> 00:02:07.759
Winterfell will win the Last War against Cersei,
unseating her from the Iron Throne.

00:02:07.759 --> 00:02:11.400
Addressing those who survived last episode's
battle, Dany declares what the North will

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:13.180
do to Cersei when they sack King's Landing:

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:15.400
"We will rip her out root and stem."

00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:17.480
It probably won't be all that simple.

00:02:17.640 --> 00:02:21.680
And if and when Cersei is booted from the
Throne Daenerys wants so much, who will be

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:23.139
the one to actually occupy it?

00:02:23.139 --> 00:02:25.989
At this point, the battle for the Iron Throne
is anyone's game.

00:02:25.989 --> 00:02:30.379
Jon Snow, whose real name is Aegon Targaryen,
is technically the rightful heir, but he's

00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:33.140
never expressed interest in ruling the Seven
Kingdoms.

00:02:33.409 --> 00:02:36.960
His aunt Dany, who is next in line to the
Throne, doesn't have as strong a claim to

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:41.960
power but wants it so much more and would
sacrifice everything to make her dream a reality.

00:02:42.180 --> 00:02:42.720
“Not Dany.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:48.940
How about my queen?”

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:54.019
Some might try to push Jon to accept dominion,
while others may try to strike him down so

00:02:54.019 --> 00:02:56.870
the Dragon Queen can add another title to
her massive list.

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:59.300
The same can be said for what people might
do with Daenerys.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:03.700
There also exists the possibility that neither
of them will replace Cersei, and someone else

00:03:03.709 --> 00:03:06.150
like, say, Sansa will succeed the Mad Queen.

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:10.120
It isn't just the core conflict between the
powers in King's Landing and the forces arriving

00:03:10.120 --> 00:03:13.530
from the North that fans have to look forward
to on the fourth episode of Game of Thrones

00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:14.120
Season 8.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:18.240
Get ready for some tense face-offs: Jaime
will stand against his sister after turning

00:03:18.249 --> 00:03:22.719
his back on her during season 7; the Hound
will see his brother, the Mountain; and Daenerys

00:03:22.720 --> 00:03:25.480
will enter the room where her father was killed
while he sat on the Throne.

00:03:25.840 --> 00:03:29.989
History might repeat itself in two of these
instances, with Jaime going from Kingslayer

00:03:29.989 --> 00:03:34.439
to Queenslayer by ending Cersei's life, and
Dany being overcome by her father's influence

00:03:34.440 --> 00:03:36.420
and slaughtering her enemies without mercy.

00:03:36.680 --> 00:03:40.870
She did it before with Samwell Tarly's brother
and father who's to say she won't do it again

00:03:40.870 --> 00:03:42.840
when emotions run high in King's Landing?

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:46.740
"The Long Night" is a tough act to follow,
but all the pieces are in place for the next

00:03:46.740 --> 00:03:49.320
episode of Game of Thrones to be an all-time
classic.

